<article class="env-lemma" id="00H4">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00H4">Lemma <span data-tag="00H4">10.38.3</span>.</a> Let $\varphi : R \to S$ be a ring map. Let $I \subset R$ be an ideal. The set of elements of $S$ which are integral over $I$ form a $R$-submodule of $S$. Furthermore, if $s \in S$ is integral over $R$, and $s'$ is integral over $I$, then $ss'$ is integral over $I$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
